// OauthCallback OAuth provider callback
//
// Redirect URI to register at the provider (`{EB_PUBLIC_URL}/callbacks/{provider}`). Public: the provider sends the browser here with `code` and `state`; EmailBridge checks the single-use state, exchanges the code (PKCE), stores the encrypted tokens on the account, writes an `account.oauth.connected` audit record and redirects (`302`) to the admin account page with `?oauth=connected`. Every failure (consent denied, expired state, exchange error) also redirects, with `?oauth_error=1`. An unknown provider is a plain `404`.
