// CreateAccountWithBody Register account
//
// Registers a mailbox in the active organisation. Unless `skipVerify` is true (or the provider is `gmail` / `graph`), EmailBridge first logs in to IMAP and SMTP with the given settings and saves nothing when either fails (`502 mail_auth_failed` / `mail_connect_failed` / `mail_tls_failed` / `mail_protocol_error`, `504 mail_timeout`); the test counts against the verify limit of 5 per minute per organisation. Passwords are encrypted at rest and never returned. `metadata` is your own free-form object (at most 32 keys, values string ≤ 1024 bytes, number, boolean or null, ≤ 8 KB as JSON); invalid metadata is `422 validation_failed` with `errors[].path` = `body.metadata.<key>` (or `body.metadata` for the key count and size). A mailbox can instead authenticate through an app-only OAuth app (`oauth.appId`), another account's OAuth token (`delegated`) or the credential server (`auth.useAuthServer`). The account starts in state `new`; a sync node picks it up within seconds. Requires `accounts.write` (owner, admin, operator; API keys `accounts:write`, not account-bound). Emits `account.added` and writes an `account.create` audit record. Supports `Idempotency-Key`; returns `Location` and `ETag`.
