	// The 1×1 transparent GIF EmailBridge adds to HTML messages when the `tracking.opens` switch is on; loading it records an open for the recipient in the token and emits `tracking.opened` (with a likely-bot flag for mail-security scanners and proxies; the IP is truncated). Public: the signed token is the credential (valid 90 days by default). Never cached (`Cache-Control: no-store`). A tampered token is `403 signed_url_invalid`, an expired one `403 signed_url_expired`.
