	//
	// The `List-Unsubscribe` link of a message sent with unsubscribe headers: a small HTML page, in the recipient's language (`Accept-Language`, 9 languages), asking to confirm; its button POSTs to the same URL. Viewing the page changes nothing (link scanners cannot unsubscribe anyone). Public: the signed token is the credential.
	//
	// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with GET /u/{token} (the `UnsubscribePage` operationId).
