	// Moves the account to `deleting`, disconnects it and queues an `erasure` job that deletes every stored copy (messages, mailboxes, outbound queue, objects in S3, logs), emits `account.deleted` and removes the account; the mailbox on the mail server is not touched. Answers `202` with the job and `Location: /v1/jobs/{jobId}`; poll the job for progress. Irreversible. An account other accounts delegate to cannot be deleted (`409 delegated_in_use`). Requires `accounts.write` (API keys `accounts:write`); `If-Match` is honoured. Emits `account.stateChanged` (to `deleting`) and writes an `account.delete` audit record.
