	// Creates or replaces the organisation's AI provider settings. `apiKey` is stored encrypted and never returned; omit it to keep the stored key, send an empty string to remove it. `features` limits which operations may call the provider (default all four); `bodyMaxChars` (256-100000, default 8000) caps the text sent per call. A `local` provider needs `baseUrl` (an OpenAI-compatible server); `none` turns the AI features off and needs no model. Keys are kept per provider: switching provider keeps the old key aside (never sent to the new provider) and restores the key kept for the new one. Provider calls go through the egress policy. The AI operations also need the `ai.enabled` switch. `embeddings` (semantic search, switch `ai.embeddings`) names an OpenAI-compatible `/embeddings` endpoint: `baseUrl` and `model`, plus an own `apiKey` (same keep / remove rule); omit the block to keep it. Without a base URL an openai or local main provider is reused (default model `text-embedding-3-small` for openai); with gemini the Gemini embeddings API is used (set `model`); anthropic, xai and none need the block. Changing the embedding model deletes the stored vectors. Requires `settings.write` (owner, admin; API keys `settings:write`).
