	// Searches the text of the organisation's messages in every account (subject, sender and body text, the first 64 KiB of each body) in EmailBridge's own text index, instead of the provider's per-account search. Needs the switch `search.fullText` for the organisation (`403 feature_disabled` while it is off); accounts can opt out. Messages are indexed as they arrive; older mail after `POST /v1/accounts/{accountId}/fulltext/reindex`. `q`: words (any of them matches), `"exact phrases"` and `-excluded` words; matching is case- and accent-insensitive on whole words, without stemming. Results are ordered by relevance, then newest first, each with a plain-text `snippet` around the first match and the match positions in it (`highlights`, code points). Filter by `accountId` and by the message date (`from` / `to`, RFC 3339, inclusive). Paged with `page` and `limit` (default 25, at most 100) over the first 1000 matches; `total` is capped at 1000 (`totalCapped`). Requires the `read` permission (API keys `messages:read`; a key with only per-account scopes must name `accountId`; an account-bound key always searches its own account). Read-only; no connection to the mail servers is made.
