// Queues a background job (`account.export`) that writes every indexed message of the account — or of `folderIds`, received in `[since, before)` — as one JSON object per line (NDJSON), gzip-compressed and encrypted at rest (AES-GCM). `include` picks the content: `metadataOnly` (the default), `raw` (base64 RFC 822) and/or `attachments` (base64 parts). Answers `202` with the export, the job and `Location`; poll `GET …/exports/{exportId}` or wait for the `export.completed` / `export.failed` event, then download. At most 3 active exports per account (`409 conflict`). Needs the `export.enabled` switch (`403 feature_disabled`). Finished exports are kept 7 days. Requires `accounts.operate` (owner, admin, operator; API keys `accounts:write`, an account-bound key only for its account). Writes an `export.created` audit record.
//
