// ReindexAccountFullTextWithResponse Rebuild the account's full-text index
//
// Queues a `fulltext.reindex` job that walks the account's message index, most recently indexed first, up to `limit` messages (default 5000, at most 50 000), and adds the messages that are not in the full-text index yet (for example mail that arrived before the switch was turned on, or a folder whose UIDVALIDITY changed). Bodies are fetched from the mail server one at a time with a pause in between, so the account stays usable. While a reindex of the account is queued or running, that job is returned instead of a new one. Needs `search.fullText` on for the account (`403 feature_disabled`). Answers `202` with the job and `Location: /v1/jobs/{jobId}`; the result counts scanned, indexed, already indexed, skipped and failed messages. Requires `accounts.operate` (owner, admin, operator; API keys `accounts:write`). Writes an `account.fulltext.reindex` audit record.
