// SubmitOutboundMessageWithBodyWithResponse Submit a message
//
// Queues one message for sending through the account's SMTP server (or its gateway / Gmail / Graph API) and answers `202` with the outbound message ID and `Location`; follow it with `GET /v1/outbound-messages/{outboundId}` or the `message.sent` / `message.failed` / `message.bounced` events. The body is either structured fields (`from` — default the account address —, `to` / `cc` / `bcc`, `subject`, `text`, `html`, `headers`, base64 `attachments`) or a complete base64 RFC 822 `raw` message (optionally with an SMTP `envelope`; both at once is `422 raw_and_fields`); or a stored `template` with variables; `recipients` sends a mail merge (one message per entry, up to 100, answered as `{ "messages": [ … ] }`); `reference` replies to or forwards an indexed message. `sendAt` in the future schedules it (`state: scheduled`); `policy: atMostOnce` never resends after an unknown outcome. `dryRun: true` builds and validates without storing or sending and answers `200` (with `includeRaw=true` also the built message; a merge dry run answers `{ "results": [ … ] }`). Recipients on a suppression list are refused (`422 recipient_suppressed`), the send quotas apply (`429` with `Retry-After`), the size limit is `EB_SUBMIT_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE` (25 MiB). Send `Idempotency-Key` to make retries safe: the same key and body replays the first answer with `Idempotent-Replayed: true`. Requires `outbound.write` (owner, admin, operator; API keys `outbound:write`). An account-bound key only for its account.
