// CancelQueueItemsWithBodyWithResponse Cancel queued records by id, by filter or the whole queue
//
// Cancels records waiting in a queue by moving each one to its `cancelled` state (the same conditional update as `DELETE /v1/outbound-messages/{outboundId}`); the stream is never purged, and a worker that later pulls a cancelled record acks it without sending. Records being transmitted right now are never cancelled. Send exactly one of: `ids` (1–500, synchronous: `200` with `cancelled` and the `skipped` ones with a reason; a single id that cannot be cancelled is `409 queue_item_not_cancellable` or `404 not_found`), `filter` (at least one criterion) or `all: true` (the whole queue in the scope, `confirm` must equal the queue name). Filter and all count the matching records and start a `queues.cancel` job (`202` with `job` and `matched`; poll `GET /v1/jobs/{jobId}`); records queued after the request are never touched, and no job is created when nothing matches (`200`, `matched: 0`). Sending needs `outbound.write` (owner, admin, operator; API keys `outbound:write`), webhook deliveries `webhooks.write` (`webhooks:write`); the caller's account / endpoint limits are kept by the job. System mail and `scope: all` (every organisation) are instance-owner only. `EMAILBRIDGE_EVENTS` is read-only (`409 queue_read_only`). Emits no event; writes one audit entry per request and a `queues.updates` realtime message per request or job batch.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /v1/queues/{queue}/items/cancel (the `CancelQueueItems` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CancelQueueItemsWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, queue string, params *CancelQueueItemsParams, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CancelQueueItemsResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CancelQueueItemsWithBody(ctx, queue, params, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCancelQueueItemsResponse(rsp)
}

